commit 9600c8c867cc9811daf71b8f4c66063de039cd2e
Author: Liam Sands <liam.sands@voyageurgroup.co>
Date:   Mon Nov 16 20:00:47 2026 +0000

    Stop writing a VG Brain block into Cowork global instructions; quiet the hook warning for people without hooks
    
    The setup playbooks had Claude write a <!-- VG Brain:start --> block into
    the user's global instructions. Its first wording (2026-05-27) told Claude
    to write proactively, use vgb-save-chat and rely on a 4 PM vgb-evening-wrap,
    all retired, and that text outlived the code in people's settings. The
    connector's connect-time instructions now carry the saving rules for
    everyone, so the playbooks no longer write a block at all.
    
    Also: the setup companion and morning-check skills, the closing setup lines,
    the README and OVERVIEW no longer present vgb-save-chat or the 4 PM wrap as
    current. The context-health line goes only to people on the autosave list
    (operators without the plugin saw a stale-hook warning in every browser
    chat), and says a gap is expected in a web browser.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012Dswk7QNoMXyhs9u8wN8QT

